    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I was using different configurations before and merging them, but it was too complicated at some point. \r\n\r\nWhen you have different depth level of objects and arrays it's just a mess to have something like that to maintain. You are lacking of context, must have multiple files open and since this is only configuration I don't think we need to separate that much the concerns as we do in our codebase.\r\n\r\nFor instance overriding some options and adding new ones from a common configuration:\r\n\r\n`prod.webpack.config.js`\r\n```js\r\nconst commonConfig = require('./common.config.webpack.js');\r\nconst prodConfig = Object.assign({}, commonConfig);\r\n\r\nprodConfig.entry = {\r\n  bundle: './dev/app'\r\n};\r\n\r\n// change the js loader config\r\ncommonConfig.module.rules[3].use[1].options = {sourceMap: false};\r\n\r\n// remove happypack\r\ncommonConfig.plugins.splice(3, 1);\r\n\r\n// add minify\r\ncommonConfig.plugins.push(new BabiliPlugin());\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have also tried the \"duplication\" strategy like `create-react-app` does. It is also too complicated to maintain when you update the configuration you have the replicate all the changes in between configurations.\r\n\r\nIf we really want to separate configurations, we should look https://github.com/Fitbit/webpack-config",
    "commit_id": "66abe76bdffbd27a24a69cd346ba784cc1e3183e",
    "created_at": "2017-07-03T12:16:39Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@\n+/* eslint import/no-commonjs: 0 */\n+const path = require('path');\n+const without = require('lodash/without');\n+\n+const webpack = require('webpack');\n+const ExtractTextPlugin = require('extract-text-webpack-plugin');\n+const HtmlWebpackPluging = require('html-webpack-plugin');\n+const BabiliPlugin = require('babili-webpack-plugin');\n+const AutoDllPlugin = require('autodll-webpack-plugin');\n+const HappyPack = require('happypack');\n+\n+const __DEV__ = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development';\n+const clean = arr => arr.filter(item => item !== false);\n+\n+module.exports = {",
